WEBVTT

00:15.140 --> 00:19.477
That means… we wasted another cartridge?

00:21.062 --> 00:23.815
Two cars, both poison,
and one cartridge left.

00:24.566 --> 00:26.901
We can't reach the end.

00:39.205 --> 00:40.373
We're gonna die.

00:42.000 --> 00:42.834
Right?

00:43.793 --> 00:45.795
We're definitely gonna die now!

00:47.839 --> 00:50.300
- I'm sorry.
- It's not your fault.

00:52.135 --> 00:53.470
I'm not blaming anyone.

00:54.637 --> 00:56.639
I know it's my own fault!

01:00.518 --> 01:04.773
Why the hell did I bet on your hunch?

01:05.440 --> 01:06.941
Your father was a fraud!

01:08.943 --> 01:10.403
I'm so stupid!

01:10.487 --> 01:12.989
I knew she was the daughter of fraud!

01:14.032 --> 01:15.492
- Calm down!
- Juri!

01:17.243 --> 01:18.703
Enough already!

01:20.163 --> 01:21.081
Why?

01:23.166 --> 01:24.209
Why?!

01:24.292 --> 01:26.294
Why do I have to die?!

01:39.516 --> 01:41.726
Excuse me.

01:44.687 --> 01:47.482
We just passed Jimbocho Station,

01:48.108 --> 01:51.277
so we're near where
the trains run in parallel.

01:52.028 --> 01:56.199
If the train we saw earlier
is still traveling at the same speed,

01:58.118 --> 01:59.619
we'll run side by side!

02:01.287 --> 02:03.081
What's your point?

02:05.792 --> 02:07.836
So that's our only option?

02:13.049 --> 02:15.135
- Jump onto the other train?
- What?

02:15.218 --> 02:18.888
The players in the front car were dead.
No need for cartridges.

02:19.597 --> 02:22.308
The doors are open,
and the poison gas is gone.

02:22.392 --> 02:23.393
No way!

02:23.476 --> 02:27.605
We either do nothing and die here
or fight to the end.

02:27.689 --> 02:29.566
That's impossible!

02:31.442 --> 02:33.027
Follow me if you want.

03:46.017 --> 03:46.893
Let's do it.

03:51.022 --> 03:52.190
Don't be stupid.

03:52.690 --> 03:56.778
Have you lost your mind?
How are you gonna jump across?

04:01.574 --> 04:02.533
The timing's key!

04:03.826 --> 04:04.953
It's almost here!

04:11.334 --> 04:13.378
It's okay. You can do it.

04:14.045 --> 04:16.381
You definitely can. Tell yourself that.

04:17.840 --> 04:19.592
I can do it.

04:21.844 --> 04:23.972
- Get up. You can do it.
- I can do it.

04:27.308 --> 04:28.226
There it is.

04:42.991 --> 04:43.992
Get ready!

04:49.038 --> 04:50.081
Now!

05:00.174 --> 05:01.509
Here I go!

05:04.220 --> 05:05.138
Move!

05:12.562 --> 05:14.480
They're dead because of her!

05:14.981 --> 05:15.898
Move!

05:17.608 --> 05:18.568
Ryuji!

05:18.651 --> 05:19.652
Hurry!

05:29.662 --> 05:30.663
Grab him!

05:58.858 --> 06:00.693
Another train is coming!

06:50.868 --> 06:51.702
Arisu!

06:51.786 --> 06:52.787
Usagi!

07:02.964 --> 07:03.965
Look out!

07:05.758 --> 07:07.009
Usagi!

07:07.593 --> 07:08.511
Arisu!

07:09.804 --> 07:10.888
Usagi!

07:27.780 --> 07:29.615
- She was with some guy.
- Shush!

07:34.620 --> 07:36.539
This is the end of the line.

07:37.540 --> 07:38.916
Please stop the train.

07:39.000 --> 07:40.168
We gotta stop it!

07:40.251 --> 07:42.003
How do we do that?

07:42.086 --> 07:43.963
How the hell would I know?

07:44.046 --> 07:45.131
We're gonna crash!

07:47.341 --> 07:48.634
Do something!

07:48.718 --> 07:50.595
- We're out of time!
- Hang on!

07:55.141 --> 07:56.642
That's the accelerator!

07:56.726 --> 07:57.727
Then this one!

08:02.398 --> 08:03.983
It's too late!

08:39.393 --> 08:41.771
Excuse me. What about these?

08:43.648 --> 08:45.525
Can you use these?

08:49.487 --> 08:53.157
Support braces.
Maybe I can use them in a game.

08:53.908 --> 08:55.409
- Thanks, Taro.
- Great.

08:56.410 --> 08:57.370
We found one!

08:57.453 --> 09:00.373
Ryuji, look what we got!

09:03.376 --> 09:05.419
- Would you like to try it?
- Yeah.

09:06.587 --> 09:07.588
All right.

09:08.256 --> 09:09.465
- One, two…
- One, two…

09:10.049 --> 09:10.925
Okay.

09:21.018 --> 09:22.186
Hang in there, Arisu!

09:36.617 --> 09:37.618
Arisu.

09:38.619 --> 09:41.998
Please. You're the only one
who can stitch him up.

09:43.666 --> 09:45.835
There's no way I can do that.

09:46.544 --> 09:47.545
You can.

09:49.755 --> 09:51.799
You stopped my leg from bleeding.

09:52.550 --> 09:55.261
See? It's all better now.

09:55.845 --> 09:59.223
Bleeding's one thing.
Stitches are totally different!

10:01.100 --> 10:03.853
This was all I could find.

10:03.936 --> 10:05.146
A sewing kit.

10:05.229 --> 10:06.939
Stitch him up with that?

10:07.023 --> 10:08.524
It's all I could find.

10:09.191 --> 10:10.192
You can do it.

10:11.068 --> 10:11.902
Please.

10:12.903 --> 10:15.239
Alcohol and water for disinfection.

10:17.450 --> 10:18.909
Come on, hurry!

10:18.993 --> 10:20.119
He's gonna die!

10:21.537 --> 10:23.873
Arisu? Arisu!

10:32.381 --> 10:34.717
Hey! That's for disinfection!

10:35.676 --> 10:36.969
It stops the shaking.

12:05.850 --> 12:07.101
You should sleep.

12:09.103 --> 12:10.187
What about you?

12:11.689 --> 12:12.690
You were crying.

12:29.081 --> 12:30.082
Like you…

12:32.918 --> 12:34.712
I keep having the same dream.

12:39.300 --> 12:41.218
Something you can't forget?

12:43.929 --> 12:44.930
I…

12:47.224 --> 12:49.059
I was obsessed with death.

12:51.061 --> 12:52.062
That's why…

12:55.858 --> 12:57.777
I crossed a line…

12:59.987 --> 13:01.363
I shouldn't have.

13:01.906 --> 13:03.157
That's all for today.

13:08.621 --> 13:09.830
Professor Matsuyama.

13:11.081 --> 13:13.000
I read your paper.

13:13.083 --> 13:14.418
It was fascinating.

13:16.629 --> 13:18.964
You're interested in mental illness?

13:19.757 --> 13:23.803
No, I mean the part that says
stimulating a part of the temporal lobe

13:23.886 --> 13:26.180
can reproduce near-death experiences.

13:34.063 --> 13:38.859
You're the only one at this university
who has shown interest in that.

13:40.194 --> 13:44.698
I read that near-death experiences
might give us a glimpse of the afterlife.

13:46.033 --> 13:48.369
Yano, do you believe in an afterlife?

13:49.203 --> 13:51.497
I want to experience it myself.

13:52.331 --> 13:53.749
- Experience it?
- Yes.

13:54.250 --> 13:57.336
I hope you'll prove
that the world of death is real.

13:59.171 --> 14:01.090
There's only one way to do that.

14:01.841 --> 14:02.758
What is it?

14:04.510 --> 14:07.096
To have a near-death experience.

14:16.856 --> 14:18.023
With this drug?

14:20.943 --> 14:23.863
But I can't vouch for its effects.

14:38.752 --> 14:39.712
Professor,

14:41.213 --> 14:42.798
I still want to try it.

14:45.301 --> 14:46.302
But…

14:49.597 --> 14:52.683
Don't you want to discover
a world unknown to others?

14:53.434 --> 14:56.145
But it's dangerous.

14:57.813 --> 15:00.858
It's fine. I want to see it
more than anything.

15:01.692 --> 15:03.569
Please, Professor.

15:04.111 --> 15:05.070
I'm begging you.

16:44.795 --> 16:45.713
Yano?

16:47.965 --> 16:48.882
Hey.

16:49.925 --> 16:50.968
Wake up.

16:51.051 --> 16:51.927
Yano!

17:09.570 --> 17:10.988
A student was found dead

17:11.071 --> 17:14.033
after a failed experiment
at Shushikan University.

17:14.116 --> 17:17.202
Investigators are considering
both suicide and foul play.

17:17.286 --> 17:21.373
The assistant professor in charge
was suspected of assisted suicide,

17:21.457 --> 17:23.625
but there was not enough evidence
to press charges.

17:23.709 --> 17:27.129
There was an accident in which
a car collided with a guardrail.

17:27.713 --> 17:30.549
The driver, a man in his thirties,
was in cardiac arrest…

17:30.632 --> 17:33.135
He regained consciousness
but is in critical…

17:33.218 --> 17:35.262
Was it an accident or a suicide?

17:35.345 --> 17:39.141
I hear Prof. Matsuyama's car accident
was really a suicide attempt

17:39.224 --> 17:41.268
after that student's death.

17:41.351 --> 17:43.187
They say he went into cardiac arrest.

17:43.270 --> 17:46.523
Maybe he got
his wish to see the afterlife.

17:46.607 --> 17:47.608
Nice one.

17:58.202 --> 17:59.870
AFTERLIFE, SHARED CONSCIOUSNESS

17:59.953 --> 18:01.580
NEAR-DEATH EXPERIENCES

18:01.663 --> 18:02.915
NOT BOUND BY TIME

18:02.998 --> 18:05.709
WHEN THE SUBJECT'S HEART STOPS…

18:05.793 --> 18:09.171
…ONCE RESUSCITATED,
THEIR CONSCIOUSNESS RETURNS…

18:40.911 --> 18:43.205
Once you cross that line,

18:44.957 --> 18:46.083
there's no return.

18:57.427 --> 18:58.554
You can return.

19:03.976 --> 19:08.147
There's something I realized
after coming back here.

19:12.776 --> 19:13.902
Any wound…

19:16.947 --> 19:18.657
can give us a reason to live.

19:25.622 --> 19:26.623
I'm not so sure.

19:35.215 --> 19:37.342
Let's make it back to our world.

19:58.322 --> 19:59.364
Arisu?

20:01.617 --> 20:02.492
Arisu!

20:04.828 --> 20:06.288
What a relief.

20:07.789 --> 20:08.707
Sorry.

20:11.793 --> 20:14.588
When does the game start?

20:17.716 --> 20:18.926
At sundown today.

20:23.430 --> 20:24.806
We're gonna be late.

20:25.766 --> 20:28.477
No, you need to rest.

20:40.656 --> 20:42.157
You guys go ahead.

20:43.200 --> 20:45.035
No way we can do that.

20:45.535 --> 20:48.622
He's right. We can't leave you behind.

20:49.248 --> 20:53.585
Arisu, you saved me
during the fortune and zombie games.

20:54.836 --> 20:55.837
Me too.

20:56.964 --> 20:59.967
I guess you saved me too.

21:04.513 --> 21:05.514
And me.

21:56.398 --> 21:58.317
Attention all players.

21:59.526 --> 22:02.029
The semifinal games are about to begin.

22:04.656 --> 22:08.910
Survivors will be eligible
to participate in the final game.

22:10.537 --> 22:12.956
The game is Tokyo Bingo Tower.

22:41.443 --> 22:45.530
The rules are as follows.
Play bingo on Tokyo Tower.

22:48.075 --> 22:52.621
Climb Tokyo Tower and press the buttons

22:53.205 --> 22:56.541
to complete a vertical,
horizontal, or diagonal line

22:56.625 --> 23:00.045
to get bingo and win the game.

23:01.380 --> 23:05.092
Work together as a team to get bingo.

23:05.967 --> 23:07.594
Yuna, calm down.

23:08.595 --> 23:10.722
Climb slowly. Nice and slow.

23:11.765 --> 23:12.599
Come on.

23:19.022 --> 23:20.857
At the very top,

23:20.941 --> 23:24.111
there's a button
for the FREE space in the middle.

23:24.694 --> 23:26.196
Good luck.

23:55.142 --> 23:56.810
The game is Kick the Can.

23:57.727 --> 23:59.229
First can. Begin.

24:16.037 --> 24:18.999
The rules are,
return the can to its starting spot

24:19.082 --> 24:23.295
and step on it
to win the game before time runs out.

24:27.799 --> 24:30.594
There will be ten cans.

24:31.678 --> 24:34.014
So only ten people survive this one?

24:44.941 --> 24:45.942
What the hell?

24:47.486 --> 24:49.905
Some floors have escalators
that we can't use.

24:49.988 --> 24:50.864
That way!

24:56.453 --> 24:58.205
What?! It's a dead-end!

24:58.288 --> 24:59.206
Shit!

25:00.165 --> 25:01.583
This won't open either!

25:02.167 --> 25:03.168
Shit!

25:03.710 --> 25:04.628
This sucks!

25:04.711 --> 25:06.671
- Where is it?
- It's not here.

25:06.755 --> 25:09.132
- What about over there?
- No, let's go that way!

25:22.312 --> 25:23.355
All right!

25:23.438 --> 25:25.649
The can is a time bomb.

25:26.149 --> 25:28.068
Safety mechanism deactivated.

25:28.693 --> 25:30.278
Nothing's gonna stop me!

25:30.779 --> 25:35.784
The time bomb countdown begins
the moment someone picks it up.

25:35.867 --> 25:36.952
Yeah, right!

25:37.035 --> 25:38.620
DO NOT USE

25:42.290 --> 25:43.458
If you let go,

25:43.542 --> 25:45.544
the timer resets

25:45.627 --> 25:47.671
and a new countdown begins.

25:48.505 --> 25:50.215
Five goddamn seconds less.

25:51.174 --> 25:55.554
The time limit decreases by five seconds
when the holder changes.

25:57.764 --> 25:59.474
Twenty seconds left.

26:00.058 --> 26:01.059
Hey!

26:03.186 --> 26:06.106
- No way!
- We'll waste a can if no one takes it!

26:06.189 --> 26:07.482
- I can't!
- Go already!

26:07.983 --> 26:10.694
- Reset. 50 seconds left.
- The can! This way!

26:10.777 --> 26:11.695
Go!

26:12.195 --> 26:13.530
- Wait!
- Found it!

26:13.613 --> 26:14.781
Don't chase me!

26:20.954 --> 26:23.290
Reset. Fifteen seconds left.

26:28.795 --> 26:29.921
Ten seconds left.

26:38.638 --> 26:39.681
Come on!

26:47.564 --> 26:50.066
First can, game over.

26:50.984 --> 26:54.988
The can exploded, so no one won this time.

26:56.239 --> 26:57.866
Nine cans left.

27:01.369 --> 27:02.787
Second can. Begin.

27:29.189 --> 27:30.398
Look out!

27:38.490 --> 27:41.451
There's no chance of winning on your own.

27:42.243 --> 27:44.412
- Teammates relay cans.
- Natsu!

27:44.496 --> 27:46.081
- Rei!
- Then we score goals.

27:48.500 --> 27:50.085
- This is impossible.
- Wait!

27:51.336 --> 27:53.129
- Help! Take it!
- Not so fast!

27:53.213 --> 27:55.924
Reset. Fifty seconds left.

27:58.885 --> 28:01.763
- Reset. Forty-five seconds left.
- Go, Big Sis!

28:01.846 --> 28:03.765
- Hurry!
- Got it!

28:05.350 --> 28:08.520
- Nine cans are left, and eight of us.
- Hey, wait!

28:08.603 --> 28:09.562
Found you!

28:11.106 --> 28:12.315
- Hey!
- Hey!

28:14.442 --> 28:15.402
Gimme that!

28:15.902 --> 28:16.903
Give it to me!

28:16.986 --> 28:17.862
Shion!

28:17.946 --> 28:19.114
Let go!

28:19.197 --> 28:20.490
- Arisu!
- Down here!

28:33.545 --> 28:35.505
Second can, game over.

28:36.172 --> 28:41.302
Cans will explode
when subjected to violent impacts.

28:41.386 --> 28:42.387
Shit!

28:43.388 --> 28:45.223
Eight cans left.

28:52.355 --> 28:53.690
- Arisu!
- Take it down!

28:54.941 --> 28:55.775
Reset.

28:55.859 --> 28:57.318
Fifty seconds left.

28:58.737 --> 29:00.321
Damn you!

29:02.157 --> 29:02.991
Arisu!

29:04.909 --> 29:06.745
Wait, damn you!

29:07.829 --> 29:08.705
Kazuya!

29:10.206 --> 29:14.085
Either they die, or we die.
One or the other!

29:14.586 --> 29:16.546
- No time to hesitate!
- Get him!

29:16.629 --> 29:17.505
Go!

29:18.006 --> 29:19.466
Okay! Come on, let's go!

29:20.717 --> 29:21.718
Hurry!

29:22.802 --> 29:23.887
Move, damn you!

29:27.474 --> 29:28.349
Hand it over!

29:28.933 --> 29:30.685
Stop!

29:34.773 --> 29:35.732
Sachiko!

29:35.815 --> 29:36.816
Me?

29:39.152 --> 29:40.069
Get her!

29:40.153 --> 29:42.530
Reset. Twenty seconds left.

29:44.616 --> 29:45.700
Pass it!

29:47.410 --> 29:48.453
Let me go!

29:49.496 --> 29:50.497
Let go!

29:51.372 --> 29:52.916
Ten seconds left.

29:56.377 --> 29:57.962
Go, Sachiko!

30:05.929 --> 30:08.056
Third can, game cleared.

30:13.102 --> 30:14.354
Thank you.

30:16.481 --> 30:17.565
Ladies first.

30:23.196 --> 30:27.325
Please wait in the elevator
if you have won.

30:27.408 --> 30:29.494
All right, that's the first person.

30:43.299 --> 30:44.968
Seven cans left.

31:00.108 --> 31:00.984
Himari!

31:03.528 --> 31:04.654
Help me, Usagi!

31:05.280 --> 31:06.906
Ryuji, I'll go help her.

31:46.279 --> 31:47.196
Himari!

31:56.581 --> 31:57.415
It's okay.

31:57.999 --> 31:59.667
Just hold on to me.

32:16.184 --> 32:17.685
- It's okay!
- Look out!

32:21.147 --> 32:22.148
Himari!

32:39.707 --> 32:40.750
You can do it.

33:16.285 --> 33:18.037
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

33:19.872 --> 33:20.873
I'm fine.

33:22.750 --> 33:24.252
Let's take it to the end.

33:24.335 --> 33:25.503
Okay.

33:29.841 --> 33:30.842
Hey!

33:35.888 --> 33:36.973
Hey!

33:37.557 --> 33:40.018
Let go, you asshole!

33:41.352 --> 33:42.937
- Shit!
- Go on ahead.

33:43.021 --> 33:44.605
Let's win this together.

33:45.523 --> 33:48.151
- Reset. Fifty seconds left.
- Shit! Let go!

33:48.234 --> 33:49.527
No way, asshole!

33:57.827 --> 34:00.246
Sorry!

34:00.329 --> 34:02.165
- Hey, stop!
- Let go!

34:02.248 --> 34:05.293
- Please!
- Goddamn son of a bitch!

34:06.711 --> 34:07.879
Stop it!

34:13.551 --> 34:14.385
Tetsu!

34:15.094 --> 34:16.429
- Go!
- What?

34:16.512 --> 34:18.181
Just go! Hurry!

34:18.264 --> 34:21.350
Get back here, damn you!

34:28.566 --> 34:29.400
Yes!

34:30.902 --> 34:33.946
- It's a fake, goddammit!
- Shit!

34:41.996 --> 34:42.997
There you are.

34:44.457 --> 34:45.458
Wait!

34:47.210 --> 34:48.044
Hand it over!

34:49.504 --> 34:51.339
Give it to me, dammit!

35:04.310 --> 35:05.311
Shion!

35:06.395 --> 35:07.688
No!

35:25.623 --> 35:26.624
Big Sister…

35:28.876 --> 35:29.877
What happened?

35:35.967 --> 35:36.968
Shit.

35:47.687 --> 35:48.896
What is this?

35:50.648 --> 35:52.150
What the hell?!

35:53.943 --> 35:54.944
Calm down, Tetsu.

35:55.444 --> 35:57.989
I am calm. Completely calm. I'm fine.

35:59.490 --> 36:01.492
- Stay strong, Tetsu.
- Shut it!

36:05.288 --> 36:06.205
Next can.

37:19.111 --> 37:20.029
Okay.

37:34.210 --> 37:36.963
Yuna, look at me.

37:37.755 --> 37:38.589
Don't look down.

37:40.174 --> 37:41.968
I can't do this anymore.

37:44.262 --> 37:45.263
Let's keep going.

37:45.763 --> 37:47.765
Otherwise, the balls will get us.

37:49.016 --> 37:50.893
We gotta press the buttons to win.

37:51.894 --> 37:54.272
Just grab the rope.

37:55.231 --> 37:56.607
It'll be okay.

37:56.691 --> 37:57.525
See?

37:59.860 --> 38:02.613
Yes, that's it. Don't look down.

38:35.521 --> 38:37.356
- You all right?
- Thanks.

38:44.447 --> 38:47.033
Never mind me. Go on ahead.

38:48.159 --> 38:50.619
Okay. I'm gonna go win the game.

38:56.709 --> 38:58.586
Fifth can. Begin.

39:01.630 --> 39:02.465
Arisu!

39:02.965 --> 39:04.091
Hand it over!

39:05.384 --> 39:06.260
Get back here!

39:16.103 --> 39:17.313
Rei, you take it!

39:23.361 --> 39:24.987
- Let me go!
- Go for it, Rei!

39:29.867 --> 39:31.827
Fifth can, game cleared.

39:33.579 --> 39:34.580
Thank you.

39:39.168 --> 39:41.212
Sixth can. Begin.

39:46.384 --> 39:47.385
Nobu!

39:50.054 --> 39:50.888
Natsu!

39:53.349 --> 39:54.266
Tetsu!

40:07.863 --> 40:08.989
Nobu, here!

40:10.491 --> 40:11.784
Ten seconds left.

40:14.203 --> 40:16.288
Go!

40:16.372 --> 40:17.206
Okay!

40:20.918 --> 40:22.962
Seventh can, game cleared.

40:24.755 --> 40:25.673
Thanks.

40:27.216 --> 40:28.092
And I'm sorry.

40:32.012 --> 40:33.597
Three cans left.

40:33.681 --> 40:35.182
Three of us left.

40:36.183 --> 40:37.059
Yeah.

40:38.936 --> 40:42.481
I'm gonna win this one for Big Sis.

40:46.944 --> 40:48.446
Thirty seconds left.

41:01.333 --> 41:03.002
Twenty seconds left.

41:13.721 --> 41:16.891
Reset. Thirty-five seconds left.

41:23.022 --> 41:25.524
Reset. Thirty seconds left.

41:29.236 --> 41:30.070
Die!

41:37.578 --> 41:38.954
You can't have it!

41:40.289 --> 41:42.917
Reset. Twenty-five seconds left.

41:44.793 --> 41:47.713
Reset. Twenty seconds left.

41:56.722 --> 41:58.933
Reset. Fifteen seconds left.

41:59.016 --> 42:00.434
Goddamn you!

42:05.856 --> 42:06.941
Reset.

42:08.275 --> 42:09.527
Ten seconds left.

42:10.486 --> 42:12.279
It's mine!

42:12.780 --> 42:13.614
Give it!

42:13.697 --> 42:15.366
- Let go!
- Let go of my can!

42:15.449 --> 42:17.535
- My can! Give it to me!
- Get off me!

42:18.452 --> 42:19.453
It's my can!

42:23.541 --> 42:25.793
Goddammit!

42:29.838 --> 42:32.216
Eighth can, game over.

42:32.299 --> 42:35.094
Don't tell me… Natsu…

42:37.429 --> 42:38.556
No way, right?

42:40.558 --> 42:42.142
I can't take it anymore.

42:46.480 --> 42:48.274
Two people left.

43:39.116 --> 43:40.659
- One more to win.
- One more!

43:48.876 --> 43:52.046
No! I don't want to die!

43:54.048 --> 43:55.424
Look out!

43:56.133 --> 43:57.509
Taro!

44:27.623 --> 44:28.457
Hey!

44:29.041 --> 44:31.293
- Twenty seconds left.
- You go first!

44:31.877 --> 44:33.545
You can't run anymore!

44:35.089 --> 44:36.382
Go already!

44:42.888 --> 44:44.348
Wait!

44:44.431 --> 44:45.432
Arisu!

44:52.606 --> 44:53.816
Get off me, dammit!

44:57.027 --> 44:58.654
- Ten seconds left.
- Go!

44:58.737 --> 45:00.989
There's no time! Go!

45:10.416 --> 45:11.333
Arisu!

45:14.586 --> 45:16.296
Ninth can, game cleared.

45:21.343 --> 45:22.928
Now we're even.

45:26.390 --> 45:27.391
Don't worry.

45:28.684 --> 45:30.227
There's one more can left.

45:31.645 --> 45:32.896
I'll win this one.

45:34.523 --> 45:35.524
Kazuya.

47:12.788 --> 47:14.706
Safety mechanism deactivated.

47:20.337 --> 47:22.089
Goddamn you!

47:30.180 --> 47:31.932
- Kazuya!
- Go!

47:33.392 --> 47:35.060
Go!

47:39.773 --> 47:40.607
Kazuya!

47:41.483 --> 47:43.277
- Shit!
- Let go!

47:48.532 --> 47:49.825
Let go!

48:03.839 --> 48:04.965
- Stop it.
- Shit!

48:05.048 --> 48:06.717
- Enough already!
- Open up!

48:06.800 --> 48:08.385
- Stop it!
- Open up!

48:08.468 --> 48:09.303
Enough!

48:17.394 --> 48:18.270
The can!

48:18.353 --> 48:19.354
It's mine!

48:21.648 --> 48:22.566
Hey!

48:23.066 --> 48:24.234
Let me go!

48:36.246 --> 48:37.623
Asswipes!

48:49.843 --> 48:51.595
Bring it!

48:58.936 --> 49:00.020
Goddamn you!

49:24.795 --> 49:26.004
Ten seconds left.

49:38.433 --> 49:40.686
Kazuya!

50:21.351 --> 50:22.352
Bingo.

50:26.773 --> 50:29.901
CONGRATULATIONS

51:02.893 --> 51:05.187
Had your fill of this world?

51:06.730 --> 51:08.982
I brought Usagi this far, as promised.

51:09.608 --> 51:11.151
The next game's the last.

51:11.860 --> 51:14.488
You'll make sure
Arisu remains here for good.

51:16.364 --> 51:18.158
Why is he so important?

51:19.618 --> 51:22.245
He helped us win the previous games,

51:23.163 --> 51:25.999
and I became a citizen thanks to him.

51:27.626 --> 51:29.669
He'll be the ideal citizen.

51:32.089 --> 51:35.133
Who… are you?

51:40.138 --> 51:41.473
Are you the Joker?

51:46.895 --> 51:49.523
It all came back to me
after I returned here.

51:50.440 --> 51:54.152
If there's an entity ruling
the world of death, tell me what it is.

51:55.445 --> 51:56.863
You ask too much.

51:57.739 --> 51:59.950
Focus on the job you were given.

52:00.700 --> 52:02.244
You're not finished yet.

52:09.126 --> 52:11.378
Kill her in the next game.

52:12.838 --> 52:14.881
That's your final job.

52:18.802 --> 52:23.014
I'm betting he'll become a citizen
and remain in this world if she dies.

52:25.725 --> 52:27.519
That's why you're doing this?

52:33.400 --> 52:37.028
Your wish will be granted if you kill her.

52:45.704 --> 52:48.290
You'll learn who rules this world

52:49.249 --> 52:54.629
and discover the true world of death
that lies beyond here.

52:56.006 --> 52:57.799
Then you can do as you please.

52:58.800 --> 53:02.971
You can become a citizen
or return to your own world.

53:06.725 --> 53:09.311
There's no better deal if you ask me.

53:22.657 --> 53:26.161
You shouldn't use this world
for your own pleasure.

53:27.245 --> 53:30.749
I'm glad to be a citizen,
but no one brings their A game.

53:31.791 --> 53:35.337
I'll only enjoy this world
if there are skilled players.

53:36.504 --> 53:37.505
That's true.

53:38.381 --> 53:41.676
Nobody brings their A game
in my stage either.

53:42.594 --> 53:44.888
In any case, we need able citizens.

53:46.431 --> 53:50.060
So you say,
but aren't you just having fun?

53:52.520 --> 53:54.314
Yeah, maybe I am.

54:14.751 --> 54:17.170
So this is the final game?

54:21.800 --> 54:23.718
A game arena in Shibuya?

54:25.345 --> 54:27.430
I hope we get out of here alive.

54:28.306 --> 54:30.934
Remember me now and then if I die.

54:33.436 --> 54:34.437
No promises.

54:35.855 --> 54:36.690
Seriously?

54:37.649 --> 54:39.484
Then don't forget me either.

54:41.111 --> 54:43.029
I'll never forget you, Tetsu.

54:45.782 --> 54:49.411
No hard feelings
if we betray each other, all right?

54:50.704 --> 54:51.788
That's a given.

54:56.126 --> 54:57.043
All right.

55:01.172 --> 55:02.090
Let's go.

55:23.653 --> 55:25.655
I've got a bad feeling about this.

55:26.740 --> 55:27.991
Who goes first?

55:39.711 --> 55:41.296
Ladies first.

55:41.379 --> 55:42.756
No thanks.

56:43.316 --> 56:44.150
Huh?

59:15.593 --> 59:18.346
Subtitle translation by: Jason Franzman
